# case: 640-repo-helper-in-seed-image
# what: the packed-refs length check goes back to grep '^.\{4201\}', as it was
#       first written for REPO-10. On the host's GNU grep that works, and
#       tests/test-repo-git-reset.sh passes. In the seed image, musl's regex
#       allows no count past 255: grep calls the pattern an error, exits 2, and
#       the `&& lrc=3` never runs, so the check passes a line it should refuse.
#
#       Expected: both runs fail on exactly one assertion, `a long packed-refs
#       line` (the mutant sends grep's own error to /dev/null, as the real
#       code's awk does); the rest of the test file passes in the seed image. A run where that assertion PASSES means the
#       seed image's grep accepts the count (a different libc, or GNU grep
#       installed), and this patch then demonstrates nothing.
#
#       Demonstrated locally on 2026-10-29 (mutate.sh apply, then run.sh --cases
#       640-repo-helper-in-seed-image): exactly that -- in both runs, root and
#       user, `a long packed-refs line` FAILed and nothing else did; on the
#       tree without the patch the case PASSed both.
#
#       No rebuild of the sandbox image needed: the case builds the seed image
#       from Dockerfile.seed and mounts the helper from the tree.
diff --git a/repo-git-reset.sh b/repo-git-reset.sh
--- a/repo-git-reset.sh
+++ b/repo-git-reset.sh
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@
   # but 0 refuses, a failed awk included.
   if [[ -f "$dir/.git/packed-refs" ]]; then
     local lrc=0
-    LC_ALL=C awk 'length($0) > 4200 { exit 3 }' "$dir/.git/packed-refs" 2>/dev/null || lrc=$?
+    LC_ALL=C grep -q '^.\{4201\}' "$dir/.git/packed-refs" 2>/dev/null && lrc=3
     case "$lrc" in
       0) ;;
       3) die "$(shown "$dir")'s packed-refs has a line longer than 4200 bytes; use reset" ;;
